Experiment 9(a): CPU Task Simulation in C

Steps:
Open the Ubuntu terminal.
Create the C program using nano expt9.c.
Write the C program to simulate a CPU-intensive task using an infinite loop and a counter.
Save the file using Ctrl + O, press Enter, and exit using Ctrl + X.
Compile the program using gcc expt9.c -o expt9.
Execute the program using ./expt9.
Observe the counter values displayed on the terminal.
Press Ctrl + C to terminate the program.
Execute the top command to monitor CPU utilization and running processes.
Press q to exit the top command.

Result: A CPU-intensive task was simulated using a C program, and system resource utilization was monitored using the top command.
